WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.067
He's President and CEO
of the foundation

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.402
for individual rights
and expression

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.504
and co-author of the book,

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.239
<i> The Cancelling
 of the American Mind</i>

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.673
Greg Lukianoff!

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.109
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.545
All right, how are you, sir?

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.180
-Great to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.716
Thank you, sir.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.517
Well, you know why you're here
this week.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.052
This is the week
that they called

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.522
the heads of the, uh,
Harvard and Penn and MIT.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.224
They could have called a number
of other colleges

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.559
like my alma mater, Cornell,

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.261
there a bunch of assholes
up there these days too.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.896
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(LAUGHS)

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.564
But these were the three
who were called,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.432
and this is really
what you've been writing about

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:35.535
for a long time,
this is what your book is about.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.304
We quoted you,
your organization FIRE

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:42.208
a few weeks ago in an editorial,
because it was about campuses

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.843
and where the free speech
was what--

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.812
First of all,
what does FIRE stand for?

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.480
"A Foundation
for Individual Rights

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.547
-and Expression."
-BILL MAHER: Okay.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:49.916
Yeah, we're 25 years old
this year.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.017
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-BILL: Okay. Oh, wow!

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.253
I didn't know
they were already that, okay.
So...

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.223
So, I remember
when we did the piece, the--

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.293
at the absolute bottom
of the list.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.362
Th-- They got a negative score.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:03.429
-BILL: Was Harvard?
-Harvard, yeah.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.097
And right next to them was Penn?

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.198
GREG LUKIANOFF: Yep.

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:08.100
So, these are two
of the colleges

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.104
-who are now on team Hamas?
-GREG: Yeah.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.673
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.709
Is that a coincidence
or what is the connection?

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.212
(CHUCKLES) Well, this is--
I mean they kind of got

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.247
what they had coming,
because they-- they had to go

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.782
in front of Congress
and convince them

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:25.485
that like, "Actually
now were good on free speech,"

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.553
and nobody believed them.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.056 line:0%
Harvard, you know,
it earned its position
at dead last.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.124 line:0%
And I always give the example.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.492 line:0%
You know, when it comes
to Harvard,

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:35.127 line:0%
Carole Hooven for example,
she's someone who was on a show,

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.163 line:0%
she was promoting
a book about testosterone,

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.398 line:0%
she made the point
that we should be kind

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.333 line:0%
and compassionate
toward trans people,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.401 line:0%
use their pronouns,

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.104
but we can't pretend
that biological sex isn't real.

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.874
And the D.I. administrator
at Harvard,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.041
you know,
started complaining about it.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.777
Suddenly students
were boycotting her class

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:51.878
and writing petitions.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:55.247
And she was-- She left Harvard
because of the environment.

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.650
And so nobody could actually
take seriously the idea

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.318
that they-- they believe
in free speech.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.289
Meanwhile, the president of Penn
after her disastrous performance

00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:05.191
comes out and says,
"Oh, you know what?

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.660
We're not actually going to have
our policies match

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.262
constitutional
standards anymore."

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.464
And it's like, no, you've been
letting administrators

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.033
clamp down on speech
for decades now,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.501
this will only make it worse.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.604
Okay, but the connection
between...

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.138
-GREG: Yeah.
-...supporting Hamas...

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.440
-GREG: Yeah
-...and the lack of free speech.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:22.775
-Yeah.
-Let's get into that,

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:23.876
-GREG: Yeah.
-...because I want to read

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.678
this is what the congresswoman,
who was grilling--

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.581
Elise Stefanik.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.750
(SCOFFS) Who has her own issues
with speech by the way.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:33.252
-(GREG CHUCKLES)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:37.123
Okay, "New York State used to be
a normie".

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:42.428
Okay, but she loves Trump now.
She's asked the Penn person,

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:46.665
"Does calling for the genocide
of Jews violates Penn's rules

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.367
or code of conduct, yes or no?"

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.703
Now, I'm a free speech person
like you are.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.938
-Yeah. Yeah.
-BILL: And I'm also team Israel.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:54.607
-GREG: Yeah.
-So let's just get real
about this.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:55.674
GREG: Sure.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.143
Calling for the genocide
of Jews,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.311
one of them I think it was
the Penn person said,

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.013
-"I've not heard that."
-GREG: Mmm-hmm.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.282
In other words,
"How explicit is it?"

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.484
Because when I break down
the phrases that I hear.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.453
-First, there's the "intifada."
-GREG: Yeah.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.520
There are a lot of people
who say

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.588
"You shouldn't say that,"

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.424
-I disagree. Free speech.
-GREG: Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.494
Intifada, that's one of those
vague terms like "Jihad,"

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.763
it probably means violence,
but you know what,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.764
-it's just-- "uprising..."
-(ALL LAUGHING)

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.399
...whatever,
give you the benef--

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.501
Okay, then there's
"From the River to the Sea."

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:23.602
GREG: Yep.

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:26.205
Okay, that's a little more
genocide-y.

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:27.306
-But, you know.
-(LAUGHS)

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.374
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.075
Let's give
the benefit of the doubt,
it could be,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.678
"Well we just want
the Jews to move, not die"

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.581
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:36.815
Where they're gonna move to,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.818
I'm going to address that
next week, in our, for our--

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.287
Our season finale is next week,
by the way.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.721
-It is true.
-(GREG LAUGHS)

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.625
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.593
As you can see
the excitement is building.

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:49.662
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-(GREG LAUGHING)

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.298
And then there's a phrase,
"by any means necessary."

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:56.335
Okay, now...
now I'm kind of peeing my pants.

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.204
-GREG: Yeah.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.440
Right, and I'm not even Jewish,
but come on.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.774
(LAUGHS)

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.642
"By any means necessary,"

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.878
that-- So, where do you draw
the line here

00:04:05.944 --> 00:04:07.213
and what do you say
is free speech,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.447
and what should not be allowed?

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:11.417
Well, w--
The First Amendment actually
gives a lot of guidance on this,

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:14.019
and one thing that's been
horrifying over the past month

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:16.689 line:0%
is seeing a lot of unprotected
speech on campus.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.991 line:0%
We're seeing things that cross
the line into true threats,

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.726 line:0%
discriminatory harassment,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.095 line:0%
we're seeing things
that actually aren't protected.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:28.134 line:0%
But merely expr--
offensive expression
like saying "intifada",

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.736
that is absolutely protected.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:34.140
But can saying things like that
be part of a pattern of threats,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.241
or harassment?

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.944
Of course, it can be,
and it was kind of embarrassing

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.445
to watch
these university presidents

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.180
of the top institutions
in the country

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.049
not being able
to answer that clearly.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:44.950
Right, see what irks me
is that,

00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:47.153
look, I'm always gonna be
on the side of

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.754
as far as you can push
free speech.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.122
-GREG: Yep.
-And of course, as you say,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.726
there's already limits to some--
speech, violence and stuff,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.228
or you can fire
in a crowded theatre--

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.762
Okay, so it's not absolute.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.664
What bothers me
is the double standard.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.667
-GREG: Oh, my God, yeah.
-That. can you imag-- I mean,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.735
okay, say they don't want
to say, "Kill the Jews"...

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.337
-GREG: Mm-hmm.
-...but I certainly have heard

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.439
-chanted "Fuck the Jews."
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:10.543
"Fuck the Jews," can you imagine
saying "Fuck the--"

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.245
and any other-- I'm not
gonna say any other group

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.015
because they'll clip the tape
and I'll live with that forever.

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:20.819
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:25.591
I just-- I cannot think
of any other group...

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.659
-GREG: Oh, yeah.
-..that you could say,

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.794
"Fuck the blank," and have it
be acceptable.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.464
The double standards on campus,
we talk about this in canceling,

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.965
we talk about this at FIRE
all the time.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:34.734
The double standards
are astounding,

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.270
but you have to have them
when you have policies like this

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.371
because if they actually

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:42.608
enforce them against everybody,
they wouldn't last a second.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.443
Yeah, I-- you know.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.746
I honestly think the kids...

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.348
I think they're...
You know that phrase,

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.017
-"Useful idiots".
-GREG: Yeah.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.485
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.121
The bigger scandal here is
that these are the biggest,

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.356
most esteemed colleges
in the country,

00:05:57.456 --> 00:06:00.326
and they've raised
a bunch of fucking idiots.

